{"causes": ["The robust Athenian democracy fostered an environment of *parrhesia*, or freedom of speech, which was essential for the development of Old Comedy's critical nature.", "The political polarization and societal anxieties generated by the protracted Peloponnesian War provided abundant material and impetus for satirical playwrights like Hermippus.", "The established traditions of public festivals, such as the Dionysia and Lenaia, offered institutionalized platforms for dramatic competition and biting political commentary."], "effects": ["Hermippus's plays significantly contributed to the vibrant political discourse and sharp social critique that defined Old Comedy in classical Athens.", "His high-profile prosecution of Aspasia offers a rare and crucial glimpse into the legal and social vulnerabilities of prominent women and foreign residents in 5th-century BCE Athens.", "The direct and often harsh satirical attacks by Hermippus and his contemporaries influenced public opinion and shaped the reputations of leading Athenian figures."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "old-comedy", "sourceName": "Old Comedy", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "hermippus", "targetName": "Hermippus", "context": "Hermippus was a prominent practitioner and influential writer within the genre of Old Comedy, active in Athens during the late 5th century BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "hermippus", "sourceName": "Hermippus", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "ancient-athens", "targetName": "Ancient Athens", "context": "Hermippus's entire theatrical career and political activities were centered in Ancient Athens during the 5th century BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "hermippus", "sourceName": "Hermippus", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "pericles", "targetName": "Pericles", "context": "Hermippus critically lampooned Pericles in his comedies, notably in *Moiros*, around 430 BCE, influencing public perception of the statesman."}, {"sourceSlug": "hermippus", "sourceName": "Hermippus", "verb": "CAUSES"